{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["Since he said 'he enlarges Sheol,' he said 'the dead whom you killed will awake.' The meaning is the children of the slain; therefore the words יקומו and יקיצו lack yod, for it is like וייקץ יקץ — its root." "R. Yeshu'ah said: Had you but placed weight upon your grave, there the dead would awake and be at rest." "<b>They that shake you</b> — like 'and it did not move from it' [i.e., the root is זע, 'to move']."], :book :habakkuk, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {1 "The quoted Aramaic/Hebrew phrase is textually difficult; rendered hyper-literally. The speaker's identity is uncertain but rendered as given."}, :source-witnesses [["<b>Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk</b>- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"] ["Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:48:52.638210602Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}